---
title: Package Signing
order: 8
description: pacman-key --init, --populate, --recv-keys
tags: [pacman, key, gpg, signing, keyring, trust]
---

pacman uses GnuPG to verify package signatures. The keyring must be
initialized and populated for package installation to work.

@code bash
# ---- keyring initialization ----

pacman-key --init                         # initialize the keyring
pacman-key --populate archlinux           # add Arch Linux keys
pacman-key --populate artix               # add Artix Linux keys

# both at once (typical Artix setup)
pacman-key --init
pacman-key --populate archlinux artix

@code bash
# ---- managing keys ----

# list keys
pacman-key --list-keys                    # all keys
pacman-key --list-sigs                    # keys with signatures

# receive a specific key from a keyserver
pacman-key --recv-keys KEYID
pacman-key --finger KEYID                 # show fingerprint

# locally sign a key (trust it)
pacman-key --lsign-key KEYID

# delete a key
pacman-key --delete KEYID

@code bash
# ---- refresh and update keys ----

# refresh all keys from keyserver
pacman-key --refresh-keys

# update the keyring packages (often fixes key issues)
pacman -Sy archlinux-keyring artix-keyring
pacman -Su

@text
Common key-related error messages:

@code bash
# "error: GPGME error: No data"
# or "error: required key missing from keyring"

# Fix: re-initialize and re-populate
pacman-key --init
pacman-key --populate archlinux artix

# "error: <package>: signature from ... is unknown trust"

# Fix: receive and sign the specific key
pacman-key --recv-keys KEYID
pacman-key --lsign-key KEYID

# "error: <package>: signature from ... is marginal trust"

# Fix: locally sign the key to fully trust it
pacman-key --lsign-key KEYID

@code bash
# ---- signature verification settings ----

# /etc/pacman.conf
# SigLevel = Required DatabaseOptional
#   Required         = packages must be signed
#   DatabaseOptional = database signatures are optional
#   TrustAll         = trust any key (dangerous, never use)
#   PackageRequired  = only packages need signatures
#   Never            = disable checking (dangerous)

@text
If you are having persistent key issues:

@code bash
# nuclear option: rebuild the entire keyring
rm -rf /etc/pacman.d/gnupg
pacman-key --init
pacman-key --populate archlinux artix

# ensure correct time (wrong clock causes verification failures)
date
# if wrong, sync time:
ntpd -qg                                 # one-shot time sync
# or if using chrony/openntpd
rc-service ntpd restart

@text
The keyring is stored in /etc/pacman.d/gnupg/. It is a standard GnuPG
directory. The archlinux-keyring and artix-keyring packages provide the
master keys and packager keys for their respective repositories.
